{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197252-healing","id":1197252,"title":"Healing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-19T10:26:25-07:00","id":1197252,"title":"Healing","content":"I\u2019m still trying to get my head around Healing, especially in Origins.<br /> <br /> Apart from letting time take its course (2 days for Bruised, 2 weeks for Injured and Maimed), I see only two ways for wounds to Heal:<br /> <br /> 1. First Aid, as described in the Combat chapter. Once per session, after combat, a character can downgrade one and only one wound on themself or someone else using Reason + Medicine (which I assume means Intellect + Medicine). A wound can only be downgraded once.<br /> <br /> 2. Healer Knacks, especially Damage Conversion, which allows essentially unlimited healing. Also, the write-up of Damage Conversion does not talk about making a roll or spending Momentum. It is simply an action, which presumably can be performed either in or out of combat. This means that a Healer with Damage Conversion will automatically heal up the entire party after every combat.<br /> <br /> I see no other way in Origins to perform healing. I have no idea what something like \u201cSurgeon with the Hands of God\u201d would be useful for, since there are no rule mechanics for surgery. Same with \u201cDoctor\u2019s Kit\u201d since \u201cDamage Conversion\u201d seems to work automatically without equipment, so taking \u201cDoctor\u2019s Kit\u201d would be pointless.<br /> <br /> Is there something I\u2019m missing? Some way to heal people with a skill roll or complex action, beyond the \u201cone wound once per session\u201d of First Aid? Otherwise, I know that my players will have one character with Healer permanently set to \u201cDamage Conversion\u201d and another with a single point of Medicine Skill to do First Aid if the Healer gets Taken Out (using Momentum to add enough dice to get enough successes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T10:48:14-07:00","id":1197261,"title":"","content":"Surgeon with the hands of god is probably for complex actions with intervals. And Doctor's kit gets applied as soon as someone takes damage, instead of you needing to use an action later. Also I think Damage conversion does need a roll. It applies when you use the first aid action is my reading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T12:02:22-07:00","id":1197284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197252-healing?p=1197261#post1197261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Surgeon with the hands of god is probably for complex actions with intervals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but what kind of operation would this be? If it\u2019s to heal an injury, Damage Conversion is better. And if it\u2019s something like removing a cancer, speed is irrelevant in most situations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1197252-healing?p=1197261#post1197261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Doctor's kit gets applied as soon as someone takes damage, instead of you needing to use an action later. Also I think Damage conversion does need a roll. It applies when you use the first aid action is my reading.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Doctor\u2019s Kit has limited uses whereas Damage Conversion is unlimited. Since an Origin character only has one knack and can\u2019t change that knack during a session, I can\u2019t see anyone preferring Doctor\u2019s Kit as their single choice.<br /> <br /> And actually, I was thinking of the Bare Minimum knack, which again seems pointless in comparison to Damage Conversion, if Damage Conversion doesn\u2019t need a roll.<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s possible that Damage Conversion *does* need a roll, or possibly the expenditure of Momentum, both of which would make it less overpowered. But if so, the description should say so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T04:48:53-07:00","id":1197557,"title":"","content":"I'd be tempted to put surgery and the like as a crafting project (Or just a complex action).<br /> <br /> Also, I'm pretty sure that Damage Conversion will only work once per Injury. So it's great if you're just Bruised, and not bad if you're Injured. But Maimed is still going to stick around 2 weeks as an Injured box. Compared to Doctor's Kit: Emergency Operation that just clears Maimed entirely (And Doctor's Kit has the advantage of not taking an action - You can still be contributing while healing. In fact, you can heal two -1 injuries while attacking someone, as one action).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}